{{also|daylights}}
==English==

===Etymology===
From {{m|en|day|}} + {{m|en|light|}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈdeɪlaɪt/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-daylight.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|daylights}}

# The light from the [[Sun]], as opposed to that from any other source.
# A light source that [[simulate]]s daylight.
# {{label|en|countable|photometry}} The intensity distribution of light over the visible spectrum generated by the Sun under various conditions or by other light sources intended to simulate natural daylight.
# The period of time between sunrise and sunset.
#: {{ux|en|We should get home while it's still '''daylight'''.}}
# [[daybreak|Daybreak]].
#: {{ux|en|We had only two hours to work before '''daylight'''.}}
#* '''1835''', Sir {{w|John Ross (Arctic explorer)|John Ross}}, Sir {{w|James Clark Ross}}, ''[http://books.google.com.au/books?id=SdQBAAAAYAAJ Narrative of a Second Voyage in Search of a North-west Passage &hellip;, Volume 1]'', pp.284-5
#*: Towards the following morning, the thermometer fell to 5&deg;; and at '''daylight''', there was not an atom of water to be seen in any direction.
# [[exposure|Exposure]] to public [[scrutiny]].
#: {{ux|en|Budgeting a spy organization can't very well be done in '''daylight'''.}}
# A clear, open space.
#: {{ux|en|All small running backs instinctively run to '''daylight'''.}}
#: {{ux|en|He could barely see '''daylight''' through the complex clockwork.}}
#: {{ux|en|Finally, after weeks of work on the project, they could see '''daylight'''.}}
# {{label|en|countable|machinery}} The space between [[platen]]s on a [[press]] or similar machinery.
#: {{ux|en|The minimum and maximum '''daylights''' on an injection molding machine determines the sizes of the items it can make.}}
# {{label|en|idiomatic}} Emotional or psychological distance between people, or disagreement.
#: {{ux|en|We completely agree. There's no '''daylight''' between us on the issue.}}

